 ## Overview
-Computes the gradient of the Eikonal constraint term with respect to the hash grid encoding features, enabling training of neural implicit surfaces via second-order derivative backpropagation [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard first-order gradient methods by explicitly handling the chain rule through the alpha scaling factor and optional second-order derivative tensors, supporting both "double backprop" and "second-order dOmega" implementations [S1, unofficial].
+Computes the Eikonal constraint term involving second-order derivatives of the hash grid encoding, supporting two backpropagation implementations: double backprop and second-order dOmega [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Mean Curvature Grid Computation](3126-mean-curvature-grid-computation.md) by specifically targeting the regularization of the gradient magnitude in neural implicit representations, rather than geometric curvature or divergence [S1, unofficial].
 
